n · 257 posts · 2006"},{"title":"Why Are Chimps So Strong?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/why-are-chimps-so-strong/123124","site":"T Nation · 255 posts · 2009"},{"title":"Greg: How Do You Train?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/greg-how-do-you-train/193978","site":"T Nation · 208 posts · 2013"},{"title":"Brain Candy Info?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/brain-candy-info/175317","site":"T Nation · 154 posts · 2012"},{"title":"It's Time to Speak the Truth...","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/its-time-to-speak-the-truth/163168","site":"T Nation · 130 posts · 2011"},{"title":"More Great Quotes!","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/more-great-quotes/118175","site":"T Nation · 123 posts · 2008"},{"title":"Was Jesus the First Democrat ?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/was-jesus-the-first-democrat/163030","site":"T Nation · 112 posts · 2011"},{"title":"Self Written Poetry Thread","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/self-written-poetry-thread/161131","site":"T Nation · 72 posts · 2011"},{"title":"David Beckham's Muscular Physique","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/david-beckhams-muscular-physique/208363","site":"T Nation · 71 posts · 2015"},{"title":"Bullet Proof Suit","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/bullet-proof-suit/196219","site":"T Nation · 13 posts · 2013"},{"title":"To Stop Hillary, Draft Condi","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/to-stop-hillary-draft-condi/44081","site":"T Nation · 7 posts · 2005"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Three-piece suit (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Three-piece_suit"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Style & presentation","chain":["Waistcoat covers the waistband and defines the torso","Fitted cut emphasises chest-to-waist taper","Sharper, more formal silhouette"],"effect":"direct","text":"A well-fitted three-piece suit gives a formal, structured outline and a visible waistline. People wear it to look polished and, for lifters, to show off a tapered torso."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["A three-piece suit consists of a jacket, trousers and a waistcoat cut from the same fabric. The ensemble traces to 17th-century England, when Charles II, following the court of Louis XIV, required courtiers to wear a long coat, a waistcoat, a cravat and breeches.[1]","For appearance, the waistcoat covers the trouser waistband and creates a clean line from chest to waist; tailors use darts and button placement to shape the torso and influence how tall the wearer looks.[1] Fit and cut therefore do much of the work of the look.","Waistcoats were almost always worn with suits before the 1940s, declined through the Depression, wartime rationing and central heating, and have since moved in and out of fashion.[1] On T Nation, lifters mention three-piece suits in the context of dressing well and dressing a muscular frame.[2][3]"],"infobox":[["Type","Menswear"],["Pieces","Jacket, trousers, waistcoat"],["Origin","17th-century England"],["Peak era","Before the 1940s; periodic revivals"],["Also called","Suit with vest (US)"]],"sections":[{"h":"Design","paras":["The waistcoat, called a vest in American English, may have lapels or not. Tradition leaves the bottom button undone so the wearer can sit comfortably, and a watch chain was once threaded through a middle buttonhole.[1] Waistcoats were rarely worn with double-breasted jackets.[1]","Silhouette depends on cut, darts and button placement: darts give a stronger shape, while a sack suit without them fits straighter and looser. Button position relates to the natural waistline and so to apparent height.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"History","paras":["The three-piece ensemble began at the 17th-century English court. In the late 18th and 19th centuries formal dress was simplified, and rules later loosened into the modern lounge suit.[1] The waistcoat was nearly universal with suits before the 1940s and has returned periodically as a sign of formality.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"In forums","paras":["On T Nation, posters mention three-piece suits when discussing dressing for work, shoe and belt pairings and looking \"dapper,\"[3][2] and in commentary on a bodybuilder wearing one at a gala.[4]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"17th century","event":"Charles II requires a long coat, waistcoat and cravat at the English court, the origin of the three-piece ensemble.[1]"},{"year":"Before 1940s","event":"Waistcoats are almost always worn with suits.[1]"},{"year":"1930s-1940s","event":"Waistcoat use declines with the Depression, wartime fabric rationing and central heating.[1]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Suit (clothing)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Three-piece_suit","source":"Wikipedia","year":null,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Greg: How Do You Train?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/greg-how-do-you-train/193978","source":"T Nation","year":2013,"type":"forum"},{"title":"It's Time to Speak the Truth...","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/its-time-to-speak-the-truth/163168","source":"T Nation","year":2011,"type":"forum"},{"title":"David Beckham's Muscular Physique","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/david-beckhams-muscular-physique/208363","source":"T Nation","year":2015,"type":"forum"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Feminization of Men","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/feminization-of-men/76024","site":"T Nation · 257 posts · 2006"},{"title":"Why Are Chimps So Strong?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/why-are-chimps-so-strong/123124","site":"T Nation · 255 posts · 2009"},{"title":"Greg: How Do You Train?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/greg-how-do-you-train/193978","site":"T Nation · 208 posts · 2013"},{"title":"Brain Candy Info?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/brain-candy-info/175317","site":"T Nation · 154 posts · 2012"},{"title":"It's Time to Speak the Truth...","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/its-time-to-speak-the-truth/163168","site":"T Nation · 130 posts · 2011"},{"title":"More Great Quotes!","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/more-great-quotes/118175","site":"T Nation · 123 posts · 2008"}]}